# kernel_fragment_harness_slim.config — payload-reduction variant fragment.
#
# PURPOSE: shrink the boot payload for unattended boot (docs/UNATTENDED_BOOT_PLAN.md
# step 1). Applied ON TOP of kernel_fragment.config + kernel_fragment_harness.config,
# so it only ever turns things OFF — it never contradicts a harness requirement.
#
# WHY THERE IS ANYTHING TO CUT: the base defconfig is BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_DEFCONFIG="rv32",
# upstream's general-purpose RISC-V config. It builds 199 modules totalling 21 MB into
# the rootfs of a headless FPGA harness whose only NIC is an smsc911x. Measured weight:
#
#     drivers/gpu   8971 KB   nouveau 3627 + radeon 3113 + drm 898
#     fs            3678 KB   btrfs 3235
#     net           1721 KB   bridge, stmmac (wrong NIC), ...
#     drivers/usb    948 KB   drivers/media 703, md 594, nvme 282
#     crypto         521 KB   arch (kvm) 469, lib 227, sound 160
#
# SAFETY — VERIFIED BEFORE WRITING THIS FILE: every driver the harness actually needs
# is already built IN (=y), not a module, so removing stock modules cannot break it:
#   SMSC911X=y (eth0)  UIO=y  UIO_PDRV_GENIRQ=y  SERIAL_UARTLITE=y  XILINX_INTC=y
#   RISCV_TIMER=y  MMC_SPI=y  MMC_BLOCK=y  EXT4_FS=y  OVERLAY_FS=y
# CONFIG_MODULES stays ENABLED on purpose: the out-of-tree spi-usd.ko (the user
# microSD controller, loaded by S11modules) must load, and the LEGACY variant's
# mps3_dfx.ko too.
#
# SLIM IS THE DEFAULT (2026-09-23, IMAGE lane): the default image is the one that
# goes into the 1-region blob, and the embedded initramfs only fits below the DTB
# slot at 0x8220_0000 with STRICT_KERNEL_RWX off (bottom of this file).

# --- graphics: 8.97 MB, and this board has no GPU -----------------------------
# CONFIG_DRM is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_RADEON is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU is not set
# CONFIG_FB is not set
# CONFIG_SOUND is not set

# --- filesystems the harness never mounts (rootfs is an initramfs; /persist is ext4)
# CONFIG_BTRFS_FS is not set
# CONFIG_XFS_FS is not set
# CONFIG_F2FS_FS is not set
# CONFIG_NFS_FS is not set
# CONFIG_CIFS is not set
# EXT4 stays =y — see the header; it is built in and cheap.

# --- storage/peripheral stacks with no hardware behind them -------------------
# CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_BLK_DEV_NVME is not set
# CONFIG_MD is not set
#
# SCSI cannot be switched off on its own: drivers/ata/Kconfig:18 does `select SCSI`,
# and CONFIG_ATA=y here. Verified by applying this fragment and running olddefconfig —
# CONFIG_SCSI came straight back as =y. ATA must go with it, and there is no SATA on
# this board. These three are =y (built into the kernel, not modules), so they shrink
# the Image rather than the module payload. MMC_BLOCK does NOT depend on SCSI, so the
# microSD route (§2.4 of the plan) is unaffected.
# CONFIG_ATA is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI is not set
# CONFIG_BLK_DEV_SD is not set

# --- virtualisation: no nested guests on a 32-bit soft core -------------------
# CONFIG_VIRTUALIZATION is not set
# CONFIG_KVM is not set

# --- networking beyond what the harness uses ----------------------------------
# The harness needs smsc911x (=y), lo, and WireGuard. Everything else is ballast.
# CONFIG_STMMAC_ETH is not set
# CONFIG_BRIDGE is not set
# CONFIG_ATM is not set
# CONFIG_6LOWPAN is not set

# --- image-size: retire the 104 KiB DTB cliff ---------------------------------
# STRICT_KERNEL_RWX forces SECTION_ALIGN = 1<<22 (4 MiB, the Sv32 superpage) on
# 32-bit — see arch/riscv/include/asm/set_memory.h:50-58 — which pads .init.text,
# .rodata, .srodata and .data onto 4 MiB boundaries. That alignment is why 53.6% of
# the 31 MB Image is zero bytes, and why the kernel's BSS-inclusive end sits only
# 104 KiB below the DTB slot at 0x82200000 (build.sh step 6/6 gates on exactly this).
# Disabling it drops SECTION_ALIGN to L1_CACHE_BYTES.
#
# TRADE-OFF, STATED PLAINLY: this gives up kernel W^X — .text/.rodata are no longer
# write-protected. Defensible on a lab harness behind a private network; it is a
# security posture decision, not a free win. riscv marks it optional
# (ARCH_OPTIONAL_KERNEL_RWX, arch/riscv/Kconfig:61), so it is legitimately togglable.
# CONFIG_STRICT_KERNEL_RWX is not set
